A||||3||Hawkman||Sloppy 5 speed shifter||||5||
Z||000000||Hawkman||04-28-2000||05:03 PM||||The 5 speed shifter in my '85 coupe is really sloppy.  I'm considering a replacement shifter - maybe one of the "shortened" models.<P>Could it be something else that is causing the sloppy patern?<P>Any advice?||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||04-28-2000||07:14 PM||||If you were to change the shaft to a shorter one it would not solve the slop. I'm not sure what is sloppy in your shifter, but I am guessing the cables may need adjusting/replacing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||04-28-2000||11:18 PM||||I may be wrong but mine was the same after dropping my engine and changing the clutch. I had to readjust where the shifter cables bolted to the linkages on the transmission.<BR>It was slipping out of 1st and 3rd but i adjusted that the way that would push the linkages farther. My shifter was real sloppy like in an old truck. I also re bleed my slave cylinder. Now my shifter is tight There is like a 2 - 2.5 inch "circle" the bottom of my shifter can move around in.<BR>good luck||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||04-29-2000||04:22 AM||||Rodney Dickman sells a select arm rebuild kit for our transmissions, it consists of a pin and new oilite bushings. It is real easy to install and should fix you right up!<P> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getragselect.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getragselect.htm</A> <P>Mike B.<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 04-29-2000).]||||reg||1
